    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 1d3d93541: corner_blends_keep_named_solid_restarts_at_each_level passes without a change to production code. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nThe new local pin combines corner blends with a requested helix and a tiny separate pocket. It finds added planar blend arcs at Z -4 and -8. It checks finite chained motion. It finds uncleared axial restart plunges in the tiny pocket at each depth and checks that each diagnostic names the site and depth.\n\ncargo test -p camcraft-motion --test pocket_blend_restart passed: 1 passed, 0 failed. Commit c6b2d15e9, merged through PR #2275, likely supplied the restart behavior.\n\nThis issue asks for missing coverage. That coverage is still absent upstream. The proposed test passes on unchanged production code, so the worker's mandatory red-before-fix rule prevents opening a PR. STOPPED; claim released. No production changes or commits were made.\n\nThe uncommitted pin remains in .claude/worktrees/issue-2341/crates/motion/tests/pocket_blend_restart.rs on branch issue/2341-pocket-blend-restart. Test output is local at /tmp/2341-pin-before.txt.\n",
